# {{projectName}}

A headless CMS project powered by [Manguito CMS](https://github.com/bobbykim89/manguito-cms).

## Getting started

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your credentials:

   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```

   At minimum, set `DB_URL` and `AUTH_SECRET`.

2. Install dependencies:

   ```bash
   pnpm install
   ```

3. Start the development server:

   ```bash
   pnpm dev
   ```

   The first run auto-migrates the database, seeds system roles, and prompts
   you to create the first admin account.

Alternatively, run `pnpm migrate` then `pnpm exec manguito createsuperuser` to set up without starting the dev server.

## Commands

| Command           | Description                                           |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `pnpm dev`        | Start dev server with file watching and auto-migration |
| `pnpm build`      | Run codegen and compile to `dist/`                    |
| `pnpm start`      | Start production server from `dist/`                  |
| `pnpm migrate`    | Apply pending database migrations                     |
| `pnpm validate`   | Validate all schemas and config                       |

Other CLI commands (run via `pnpm exec manguito <command>`): `createsuperuser`, `users:promote`, `users:demote`, `migrate:status`, `version:list`, `version:diff`, `version:create`, `version:retire`.

## Project structure

```
schemas/
├── content-types/    ← Content type schema definitions
├── paragraph-types/  ← Reusable paragraph block definitions
├── taxonomy-types/   ← Taxonomy (tag/category) definitions
├── enum-types/       ← Enum type definitions
├── roles.json        ← Role hierarchy and permissions
├── routes.json       ← Public API route configuration
└── versions/         ← API versions, created by `version:create` — commit this

migrations/            ← Generated database migrations

.env.example           ← Environment variable template
manguito.config.ts     ← CMS configuration
```

Your API is already versioned: it is served at `/api/v1/...` as well as
`/api/...`. Before renaming or removing a field that clients use, run
`pnpm exec manguito version:create`. See the
[schema versioning guide](https://github.com/bobbykim89/manguito-cms/blob/master/docs/schema-versioning.md).

Consumers on the unversioned `/api/...` path follow the working schema and see
a change as soon as you make it, so move them to a pinned `/api/vN` path before
you change a field they use.

Full documentation: https://github.com/bobbykim89/manguito-cms#readme
